  "clips": [
    {
      "id": "7e75559bb502f671",
      "text": "This is the Night Line on fourteen-twenty, Caliche. We are on till four.",
      "duration": 3.9,
      "file": "7e75559bb502f671.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "1d315be944a93f19",
      "text": "It's",
      "duration": 1.16,
      "file": "1d315be944a93f19.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "a550c489649722f4",
      "text": "in Caliche.",
      "duration": 1.12,
      "file": "a550c489649722f4.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "a75fe8476c9194e4",
      "text": "Cold one out there. Thirty-eight on the bank sign, and the wind has laid down.",
      "duration": 4.39,
      "file": "a75fe8476c9194e4.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "16d69fc1b62a3e6a",
      "text": "Phones are open. If you are up anyway, you might as well talk to somebody.",
      "duration": 3.99,
      "file": "16d69fc1b62a3e6a.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "3b571ed64f0acb86",
      "text": "Dolores, I believe you. Now turn the porch light off and go to bed.",
      "duration": 3.64,
      "file": "3b571ed64f0acb86.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "22cf84eb221737ec",
      "text": "This one goes out to the night crew up at the observatory. Somebody has to listen to the sky.",
      "duration": 5.15,
      "file": "22cf84eb221737ec.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "0e0fd22c82477220",
      "text": "We lost the transmitter about then. Needle went to nothing for most of a minute. Ray, if you are listening, that one is yours.",
      "duration": 7.07,
      "file": "0e0fd22c82477220.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "4502af1e0505b497",
      "text": "Jack Nicklaus, forty-six years old, took the Masters this afternoon. Thirty on the back nine. My uncle says he called it. My uncle calls everything.",
      "duration": 8.51,
      "file": "4502af1e0505b497.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "db60994a5fe4923c",
      "text": ". Night Line, fourteen-twenty.",
      "duration": 1.99,
      "file": "db60994a5fe4923c.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "c5f711fdd44ac6f5",
      "text": "Halley's comet is low in the south this week. Get out past the last streetlight and give your eyes ten minutes.",
      "duration": 6.38,
      "file": "c5f711fdd44ac6f5.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "59b96b09e3d83603",
      "text": "Smart dog.",
      "duration": 1.13,
      "file": "59b96b09e3d83603.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "ba7dc83641014488",
      "text": "That's Halley's comet, son. It's there all week. You're up late.",
      "duration": 3.61,
      "file": "ba7dc83641014488.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "fc9d380225dd1df1",
      "text": "Is your dad up?",
      "duration": 1.12,
      "file": "fc9d380225dd1df1.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "71de3c549ee31d2a",
      "text": "Folks, I want to say something. That line was dead when I picked it up. No dial tone, nothing at all.",
      "duration": 5.86,
      "file": "71de3c549ee31d2a.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "3dd0dd8c7b489770",
      "text": "I don't know who I was talking to.",
      "duration": 1.68,
      "file": "3dd0dd8c7b489770.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "3675a32435189f91",
      "text": "That's the Night Line. Thank you for staying up with us.",
      "duration": 2.65,
      "file": "3675a32435189f91.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "89a95423047e84c9",
      "text": "This is fourteen-twenty, Caliche, New Mexico, signing off until six. Good night.",
      "duration": 4.33,
      "file": "89a95423047e84c9.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "00aaa3694dcb2ea2",
      "text": "Night Line, fourteen-twenty.",
      "duration": 1.99,
      "file": "00aaa3694dcb2ea2.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "3256989421322886",
      "text": ", and the coffee in here is older than some of you.",
      "duration": 2.71,
      "file": "3256989421322886.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "96fc0822d5ea7732",
      "text": "Bank sign says thirty-six now. Warming up by Wednesday, they tell me.",
      "duration": 4.26,
      "file": "96fc0822d5ea7732.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "2f60567a966623ee",
      "text": "on the Night Line. I can see the highway out my window, and it's empty both ways.",
      "duration": 4.62,
      "file": "2f60567a966623ee.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "5e8372af00d194ff",
      "text": "I noticed that. Rattled the windows all evening, and then nothing.",
      "duration": 3.85,
      "file": "5e8372af00d194ff.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "9b70343557275f10",
      "text": "Up on a roof at this hour, they can have it.",
      "duration": 2.34,
      "file": "9b70343557275f10.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "809a8e15c163c49d",
      "text": "The government place. Nobody's been out there in years.",
      "duration": 3.24,
      "file": "809a8e15c163c49d.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "9f31a2de38646b20",
      "text": "My dad said the survey crews out there worked nights, back in forty-seven. You could see their lamps from town.",
      "duration": 6.14,
      "file": "9f31a2de38646b20.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "b86e79f630dcd30f",
      "text": "Then one summer they packed up and went, and left the lamps.",
      "duration": 3.34,
      "file": "b86e79f630dcd30f.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "a2c386a4506964aa",
      "text": ". Not long now till four, so if you've been meaning to call, call.",
      "duration": 3.62,
      "file": "a2c386a4506964aa.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "e42b27bf7f08c1df",
      "text": "Not the wind, then.",
      "duration": 1.38,
      "file": "e42b27bf7f08c1df.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "c226a8ec9adcbcd0",
      "text": "County chained that gate years ago, Dolores.",
      "duration": 2.61,
      "file": "c226a8ec9adcbcd0.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "0c079c45e01ccc2c",
      "text": "My granddad ran chain for the survey crews. Never trust one mark, he said. Sight two, and if one has walked, the other tells you.",
      "duration": 7.52,
      "file": "0c079c45e01ccc2c.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "7c599e81cb074f89",
      "text": "And if you think it's your own lamp making the shadows, put your hat over the lamp and look again.",
      "duration": 5.49,
      "file": "7c599e81cb074f89.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "c4950c0d339360e3",
      "text": "My sister ran the photo counter at the drugstore twenty years. Film doesn't care what time it is, she used to say.",
      "duration": 6.28,
      "file": "c4950c0d339360e3.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "00375e42e5ef33f9",
      "text": "But it doesn't keep, either. Not in a warm truck.",
      "duration": 2.52,
      "file": "00375e42e5ef33f9.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "7edf543d86d90a3d",
      "text": "That's about all from the Night Line. When the anthem comes on, that's me going home.",
      "duration": 4.81,
      "file": "7edf543d86d90a3d.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "e8ba09e6814280d2",
      "text": "And?",
      "duration": 0.77,
      "file": "e8ba09e6814280d2.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "968a8b0dc7bad751",
      "text": "Not past the junction. Barricade's still up. You want Roswell, go around like everybody else.",
      "duration": 5.31,
      "file": "968a8b0dc7bad751.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "58960ddd0cbbc18a",
      "text": "That European probe flew right up to the comet last month and sent back a picture of a potato. Seventy-six years we waited, for a potato.",
      "duration": 7.8,
      "file": "58960ddd0cbbc18a.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "78cbdf5c6e8f7067",
      "text": "Tell her I heard. And tell her I'm still not paying for last week's.",
      "duration": 3.93,
      "file": "78cbdf5c6e8f7067.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "6ccf5dbfb58d48fb",
      "text": "Tuesday is tax day, folks. If you haven't mailed it yet, I don't want to hear about it on this program.",
      "duration": 5.78,
      "file": "6ccf5dbfb58d48fb.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "3fb42e5d00bfcedf",
      "text": "If you're in town and you see the light on over my door, I'm in here. Lean on the buzzer during a long record.",
      "duration": 6.01,
      "file": "3fb42e5d00bfcedf.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "a964091b283552a2",
      "text": "Is it doing anything?",
      "duration": 1.34,
      "file": "a964091b283552a2.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "b1e38e8c9f6d2932",
      "text": "Well. Wave.",
      "duration": 1.31,
      "file": "b1e38e8c9f6d2932.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "2a05170c9f439106",
      "text": "in Caliche. Pumps are locked till six, so if you're low, you're low.",
      "duration": 3.8,
      "file": "2a05170c9f439106.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "a5f397cd030d7f5f",
      "text": "They do that. They're listening for something.",
      "duration": 2.49,
      "file": "a5f397cd030d7f5f.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "1b3134a26b449df6",
      "text": "Cattle report, for those of you who keep cattle and can't sleep. Feeders off again at the Roswell sale. Everybody still blames the dairy buyout.",
      "duration": 8.34,
      "file": "1b3134a26b449df6.mp3"
    },
